<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pieria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pieria is a region of Central Macedonia in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, lying between Mount Olympus and the western shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thermaic-gulf">Thermaic Gulf</a>, with Katerini as its main town. In antiquity it was the home of the Pierians and was associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muses">Muses</a>, and it was absorbed into the Macedonian kingdom early in its history. Its ancient sites include Dion, the sacred city of the Macedonians, Pydna and Methone.</p></div>
